
# The render runtime's host-node handle: an opaque wrapper around a platform node (a browser Element via bind, or an
# in-memory record on the server). Every native impl stores its concrete node in `handle`; the render runtime and apps
# only ever pass a `view` around, never a host primitive.
#
# The form is defined once per backend, with the same public shape (one `mark private` field, `handle`) and the handle
# typed as what that backend stores: native/node/view (a page-element), native/memory/view (a memory-element),
# native/browser/view and native/toolkit/view (dynamic), and native/view for any other env. The build bears the one for
# its target, so a read through a handle needs no retype at the point of the read.

bear @term/site/dom/native/{platform}/view
